Data the shell embeds
=====================

emoji.tsv    The emoji, kaomoji and symbols of the emoji panel (Super+. and
             Super+;), with their names, search keywords and skin tones.
             Generated by ../../../tools/build_emoji.py from the Unicode data
             that Debian's unicode-data and unicode-cldr-core packages install
             (emoji-test.txt, UnicodeData.txt, DerivedAge.txt and CLDR's
             English annotations; the versions are in the file's second line).
             Do not edit it by hand: run the generator, and
             `build_emoji.py --check` to see that the committed file is
             current. The kaomoji and the choice of symbols are the
             generator's own lists.

Licence of the Unicode data in emoji.tsv
----------------------------------------

emoji.tsv contains data selected and reformatted from the Unicode Character
Database, the Unicode emoji data and the Unicode Common Locale Data
Repository (CLDR).

